  "order_rationale": [
    "1. The C001 occurrence-02 grid comes first because its delivery record is clean: all 20 replicates across all four cases are `delivery_status: COMPLETE`, `comparable: true`, `state: PRESENT` and `fcl.parse: OK`, and the published `unresolved_cells` list is empty. G10(b)'s three-resolved-replicates rule is therefore satisfiable for every case by inspection of the published record, before a single call is made.",
    "2. Inside the C001 leg the within-ORIGINAL baseline row comes first, because PLAN §8a requires it - 'the baseline note is written first and is not revised afterwards' - and G8 makes that physically irreversible by pinning its sha256 into every later call record. The four baseline cells cost no calls; they are the seal the rest of the leg depends on.",
    "3. The three cross-case comparisons then follow in falsifier order: ORIGINAL vs CONTROL (D1), vs RECODING (F2), vs CARRIER (F3); and within each comparison the registers follow PLAN §8a's own order T, E, D, G. The order is the frozen plan's, not the loop's.",
    "4. The H005 rows follow in the order the published instrument emitted them, which is the instrument's own deterministic order and is not re-sorted here. Reading them second means the readings that feed the cycle-2 audit's paraphrase-invariance and premise-deletion arms already exist.",
    "5. C001 occurrence-01 is deliberately NOT in this set. Its `deepseek-flash`/`fcl` juxtaposition delivered 1 of 20 replicates COMPLETE at that occurrence's 8192/180 s ceiling and carries 19 unresolved cells, so G10(b) pre-empts marking for it; its other eleven juxtapositions would need 132 further cross-case cells, well past the declared boundary. Its cells are named `unread` - unreached by spend - and are protected as unresolved by obligation p10. They are never rendered as unresolved by inquiry.",
    "6. The published figure of 90 use-table rows counts the H005 golden and full tables separately. Their `rows` arrays are byte-identical (22 rows each, all in `daily/mini_fcl/cycle01`); the `full` scope covers 17 coordinates but yields no additional row. The reading set names those 22 distinct rows once. Reading them twice would be re-reading the same cell, which G11 forbids without a `reopen_reason`."
  ],
  "max_calls_derivation": {
    "guarded_row_cost_h005": {
      "critic": 1,
      "defender": 1,
      "judges_canonical_order": 2,
      "judges_swapped_order_G6": 2,
