        "cells": 1,
        "cost_each": 46,
        "subtotal": 46,
        "why": "one window, due at the cycle n where n mod audit.period == 0, which inside a 3-cycle budget is cycle 2 only. Planted-flaw calibration: 9 constructed rows x 2 judge seats = 18. Paraphrase invariance over a declared sample of 4 readings already on record: 4 variator calls + 2 seats x 2 paraphrases x 4 readings = 16, subtotal 20. Premise deletion over the same 4 readings: 2 seats x 4 readings = 8. Ensemble disagreement is read off existing records at 0 calls. 18 + 20 + 8 = 46."
      },
      {
        "leg": "dispatch (S4-S7 runner v2)",
        "cells": 0,
        "cost_each": 0,
        "subtotal": 0,
        "why": "both named occurrences are published and delivery-complete - H005 occurrence-01 is frozen, and C001 occurrence-02's single juxtaposition is 20/20 COMPLETE with zero unresolved cells - so `ready_coordinates` is empty and `send_round` dispatches nothing. A non-empty queue is a planned != expected discrepancy and PREFLIGHT refuses before any spend."
      }
    ],
    "max_calls": 396,
    "arithmetic": "0 + 108 + 242 + 46 + 0 = 396",
    "boundary_statement": "396 is a declared attention-and-spend boundary, not a prediction and not an adjudication. PREFLIGHT refuses a plan whose planned call count exceeds it and asserts planned == expected with provider_calls == 0. The expected spend is far lower: G10(d) is expected to remove the six T and D cross-case cells from the hot path entirely (-54), a `relation: none` from the critic ends a row at one call, and G7 runs only on a sustained ruling. Where the boundary is reached, the stop is `resource_boundary`, the unreached entries are printed as `unread`, and the record says which boundary was reached and what would reopen the question. It is never reported as the inquiry running out of things to say.",
    "audit_schedule_declaration": "An audit window is due in a cycle n where n mod audit.period == 0. With audit.period = 2 and cycle_budget = 3 that is cycle 2 and only cycle 2: exactly one window, 46 calls. §2.5 says 'every AUDIT_PERIOD cycles' without fixing the phase, so a schedule of {1, 3} is a second reading of the same words and would cost two windows. The phase is declared here, before the first call, and PREFLIGHT's planned == expected assertion refuses rather than overspending if the implementation schedules otherwise."
  },
